

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 10

                                  FOR

                         COSMIC HERDERER MUGAI







          Guido Pacifici
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  Elizabeth I, Queen of England, to her subjects in 1601:
  "You have had, and may have, many mightier and wiser princes sitting upon 
this throne; yet you never had, nor shall have any that will love you 
better."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  In spring, Mugai's attempted cast of the Tornado spell was unsuccessful.  
A strange magical counterspell seemed to have worked against his spell.
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  Mugai failed in his attempt to 
cast a Tornado spell.
  With the advent of the late summer season, Mugai cast a Bless spell.  The 
Amazonian Sea was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no 
armies in the Amazonian Sea.
  During fall, Mugai travelled to Tabora.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  Mugai tried a Skeletal Army spell, 
but bungled it.

  A diplomatic furor erupted between the Realms of Mugai (whose alliances 
are too incompatible) and Giovanna (#7), degrading their diplomatic 
relations 1 level(s)!
  Thus endeth the adventures of Cosmic Herderer Mugai for this year.


  Mugai treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Mugai Treated with Hokuto, 
but Hokuto did not react favorably to his friendly overtures.  It is hoped 
that next year, both Kings will see the wisdom of Treating.
  Mugai treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Mugai treated with his ally 
II Kahn (#6).  Mugai urged Giovanna (#7) to improve relations with his 
Kingdom, speaking eloquently of the great advantages of such an agreement.  
After some deliberation, the offer was wisely accepted by Giovanna.
  Mugai treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Mugai treated with his ally 
Agesilao (#9).

  Here is the financial report for Mugai's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 14 gold in revenue.  2 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  3
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Mugai was left with 65 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Samantha
To: Mugai

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I moved into Chirfa.
  The wet spring blossomed into early summer.  I gathered intelligence in 
Chirfa and wrote this report.  Chirfa owes allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Listening to the stories of wanderers, 
one can deduce the ownership of surrounding areas: Berga- Uga-Buga Makumb; 
Limerick- Uga-Buga Makumb; Ngara- Uga-Buga Makumb; Chaco- Uga-Buga Makumb; 
Balmwood- Uga-Buga Makumb; Silvermist- Uga-Buga Makumb.
  Approximate Taxation: 2
  There were no conspicuous characters or forces in Chirfa.
  While assigned to spying, I heard about the Screw, an interesting 
invention used by Uga-Buga Makumb (#1)'s Kingdom.  The Screw's function is 
to somewhat increase Uga-Buga Makumb's tax base.  I easily deduced how to 
make the Screw.  Now, we can use it too!  The following benefits are 
conferred by the Screw:
  The Screw helps your woodworking industry.  Its effect is to raise the 
revenue of the Kingdom by an average of 3% each gameturn.

  I also kept tabs on the characters in Chirfa and any further news is in 
the General Intelligence Report.

  With the coming of the late summer season I hired the 213th Chariots, a 
redoubtable mercenary army which had arrived in Chirfa.

  In Chirfa, Cosmic Herderer Mugai brought to bay the forces of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Samantha's armies took control of 
Chirfa practically uncontested.  Chirfa was discovered to have a tax base of 2
gold.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  I marched on Ngara 
(#604) with my command.

  Cosmic Herderer Mugai sent an invasion force into the Jungle province of 
Ngara, owned by Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  I commanded the 
attacking armies.  The defenders were commanded by the provincial garrison 
commander.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Ngara (0604):

