  DEFENDING ARMY

  I marched with my loyal troops, jaws set in terrible determination.  No 
generals were present to lead the forces of Uga-Buga Makumb.
  I seemed lucky, for I was able to convince a native tribe to aid my cause. 
But my luck turned bad when the acting commander bribed Samantha's ally to 
turn traitor, giving the acting commander a great advantage.  As the battle 
intensified, the tactical abilities of the acting commander and I seemed to 
be evenly matched and neither general could gain a tactical advantage.
  Mugai's troops were prepared to fight desperately for their homeland.
  Across the whole front, the 213th Chariots faced the 6th Garrison.  The 
13th Garrison flanked the enemy and attacked with full force.  The 213th 
Chariots fought the 6th Garrison and crumpled under the heavy pressure, 
retreating in disarray.
  Having found a weak point in the line of the host of Mugai, a final 
determined thrust finished off their opponent and won the day for the acting 
commander.
  Although the provincial garrison commander's forces were triumphant, I 
regrouped my forces and prepared to fight for Ngara.

  Thy humble servant,   Samantha


