  Samantha marched with her loyal troops, jaws set in terrible 
determination.  No generals were present to lead the forces of 
Uga-Buga Makumb.
  Samantha seemed lucky, for Samantha was able to convince a native tribe to 
aid her cause.  But her luck turned bad when the acting commander bribed 
Samantha's ally to turn traitor, giving the acting commander a great 
advantage.  As the battle intensified, the tactical abilities of the acting 
commander and Samantha seemed to be evenly matched and neither general could 
gain a tactical advantage.
  Mugai's troops were prepared to fight desperately for their homeland.
  Across the whole front, the 213th Chariots faced the 6th Garrison.  The 
13th Garrison flanked the enemy and attacked with full force.  The 213th 
Chariots fought the 6th Garrison and crumpled under the heavy pressure, 
retreating in disarray.
  Having found a weak point in the line of the host of Mugai, a final 
determined thrust finished off their opponent and won the day for the acting 
commander.  Although the provincial garrison commander's forces were 
triumphant, Samantha regrouped her forces and prepared to fight for Ngara.
  In late summer, Tao-Li (#32)'s naval forces took control of the Crabman 
